# Scilene Benchmark

This directory contains the benchmarking framework used to evaluate Scilene's recommendation engine and AI components.

The goal is to ensure every significant change is validated using reproducible experiments rather than intuition.

## Planned Structure

```
benchmark/
├── datasets/      # Benchmark datasets
├── scripts/       # Evaluation scripts
├── results/       # Benchmark results
├── baselines/     # Baseline implementations (e.g., TF-IDF)
└── README.md
```

## Purpose

The benchmark will be used to evaluate:

- Embedding models
- Recommendation algorithms
- Ranking strategies
- AI-assisted enrichment pipelines

using a common evaluation protocol.

## Benchmark Principles

- Use real published research.
- Compare against strong baselines.
- Measure improvements objectively.
- Keep experiments reproducible.
- Track benchmark history over time.

See `docs/BENCHMARK.md` for the benchmark specification.